From a5c40bf838b324e258eac6df46425e5a69bd4504 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cliffhall <cliff@futurescale.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 23:20:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat: port the skills harness (verify:skills,
 verify:skills:cli, skills:eval)

Port the MCP Inspector's skills infrastructure for #4858 Part 3:

- scripts/verify-skills.mjs, verify-skills-cli.mjs, skill-eval.mjs and
  scripts/lib/{skill-manifest,claude-cli,npm-scripts,win-shell-args}.mjs,
  with all their *.test.mjs files
- root npm scripts verify:skills, verify:skills:cli, skills:eval and
  test:scripts; yaml as a root devDependency
- docs/skill-authoring.md, with paths and provenance adapted
- a root-guards job in typescript.yml running verify:skills and
  verify:skills:cli on every push and pull request
- .claude/skills/ (kept by a .gitkeep until the first skill lands)
- un-ignore scripts/lib/, which the Python `lib/` pattern swallowed

Adapted to this repo: checkWiring reads typescript.yml, and carries two
temporary allowances (validate -> verify:format-coverage, removed by
#4864; local:gate -> verify:skills:cli, removed by #4871) that excuse a
link only while its pending script is absent and fail as stale once it
exists. The "no skills found" failure is kept, with a temporary
EMPTY_SKILLS_BOOTSTRAP allowance that fails as stale once a skill exists.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: cliffhall <cliff@futurescale.com>
